
# -----------------------------------------------|---------------------|
#           Conventional Commit Format           |  COMMIT MAX LENGTH  |
#                (Content-Focused)               |<- 1st line | body ->|
# -----------------------------------------------|---------------------|
# Common commit types for content repositories:                        |
# publish, draft, revise, edit, archive, design, asset, config         |
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
# publish  : New content going live                                    |
# draft    : New content that is not yet ready to be published         |
# revise   : Substantive content changes, additions, corrections       |
# edit     : Grammar, typos, clarity, links, formatting fixes          |
# archive  : Move old content to archives, mark as outdated            |
# design   : Visual/layout/theme changes, site structure/navigation    |
# asset    : Add/update media files                                    |
# config   : Site configuration                                        |
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
# <type>[(optional scope)]: <description>                              |
# <blank line>                                                         |
# [optional body - explain *what* and *why*, not *how*]                |
# <blank line>                                                         |
# [optional footer(s) - Issues, references, etc.]                      |
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
# Example commits:                                                     |
#   publish: Add post on Docker networking                             |
#   revise(docker-post): Expand section on bridge networks             |
#   edit(docker-post): Fix typos and broken links                      |
#   archive(2020-tutorial): Mark as outdated                           |
#   design: Update header styling for mobile                           |
#   asset: Add diagram for network topology                            |
#   config: Update Jekyll version to 4.3                               |
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
# Scope examples:                                                      |
#   - Post title or slug: (docker-post)                                |
#   - Page name: (about), (contact)                                    |
#   - Date: (2024-01-15-post-title)                                    |
#   - Section: (tutorial), (blog)                                      |
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
# Note: This template is adapted for content-focused repositories      |
# (blogs, documentation sites, etc.) and does not use semantic         |
# versioning or breaking change conventions.                           |
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
